From: Huasifei WS1610 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: RTL8221B firmware patch + pcs rate-follow

The RTL8221B SerDes requires Realtek's patch ramcode to be uploaded
after every power-up; the MTK SDK ethernet driver does this on every
boot ("RTL822x init success!"), mainline never did. On boards with
crossed SerDes pairs (Huasifei WS1610) the SerDes never locks without
it: copper autoneg completes and phylink reports "Link is Up", but no
frame is ever received.

Two parts, both mirroring the vendor SDK behaviour verified working on
this hardware (QWRT/immortalwrt-mt798x reference firmware):

1. rtl8221b_fw.c: port of the SDK Rtl8226b_phy_init() patch loader
   (nc0/nc1/nc2/uc2/uc ramcode tables), hooked into the shared
   rtl822xb_config_init() and gated on the RTL8221B PHY ID.

2. pcs-mtk-lynxi rate-follow: when a 2500base-x link resolves at a
   lower PHY speed, reconfigure the PCS line rate to 1.25G
   (1000base-x/SGMII), matching the vendor "configuring for
   phy/1000base-x" behaviour at 1GbE.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/Makefile
@@ -2,5 +2,6 @@
 realtek-y			+= realtek_main.o
 realtek-y			+= phy_patch.o
 realtek-y			+= phy_patch_rtl826x.o
+realtek-y			+= rtl8221b_fw.o
 realtek-$(CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY_HWMON) += realtek_hwmon.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY)	+= realtek.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/rtl8221b_fw.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1446 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
+/* Realtek RTL8221B-VB vendor firmware patch loader.
+ *
+ * Ported from the MTK SDK rtl822x driver (nic_rtl8226b_init.c, Realtek
+ * ramcode) as shipped in immortalwrt-mt798x. The RTL8221B SerDes requires
+ * this patch ramcode (nc0/nc1/nc2/uc2/uc segments, ~950 MMD31 writes) to
+ * be re-uploaded after every power-up. Without it the SerDes never locks
+ * on boards with crossed differential pairs (verified on Huasifei WS1610,
+ * MT7981 + RTL8221B-VB-CG: copper autoneg fine, SerDes dead, zero RX).
+ */
+
+#include <linux/bitops.h>
+#include <linux/mdio.h>
+#include <linux/phy.h>
+
+struct rtl8221b_mmd_reg {
+	u16 dev;
+	u16 reg;
+	u16 val;
+};
